  "summary": "Rough Waves (Japanese: 波濤 図 屏風) is a painting by the Japanese artist Ogata Kōrin, on a two-panel byōbu (folding screen).",
  "description": "Rough Waves (Japanese: 波濤 図 屏風) is a painting by the Japanese artist Ogata Kōrin, on a two-panel byōbu (folding screen).  The work was created c. 1704 – c. 1709, and depicts a swirl of stormy sea waves.  It has been in the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York, since 1926, when it was acquired with financial support from the Fletcher Fund.",
  "culturalContext": "Throughout the history of Japanese art, many artists have sought to convey in their works the fleeting state of rolling sea waves. The theme has been depicted not only on emakimono (handscrolls) and silk, but also on fans, byōbu and decor items.",
